Jakob Creutzig <creutzig@mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de> writes:

[weap-343.txt]

> Speaking of it, this is a very nice spoiler; however, I 
> always found the passage 'this damage can't be doubled' 
> for silver damage a little confusing.  What does this 
> mean exactly?  
> 
> ( ) If you are #twoweaponing with both weapons silver, 
>     the silver damage is only calculated once.  

No, damage from two-weaponing is calculated entirely independently for
each weapon, with the proviso that jousting does less damage with a
lance held secondary.

> ( ) If the hit damage would be doubled (e.g., Grayswandir), 
>     the silver damage is added to the result _after_ doubling, 
>     so it's not doubled.

Right. All the "this damage can't be doubled" notes are a forward
reference to the "Artifact [...] doubling" step.

(In fact, as has been noted in the past, these bonuses are actually
totalled then halved before doubling, which results in a slightly
different distribution; nothing to make a significant difference,
however.)

